b.com/surya-koritala/sigbound)\n   307→Run AI coding agents in parallel on one git repo and safely auto-merge their work — only changes that build and pass tests land.\n   308→- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n   309→- **Category:** CI/CD Integration\n   310→\n   311→### [mentor](https://github.com/smixs/mentor)\n   312→A session-insights skill for AI coding agents. Reads your local Claude Code and OpenAI Codex history and writes an /insights-style HTML report on how you work.\n   313→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   314→- **Category:** Analytics/Insights\n   315→\n   316→### [pm-manager](https://github.com/wei63w/pm-manager)\n   317→Know what to fix next — local .pm governance skill pack for AI coding agents.\n   318→- **Launch Date:** July 21, 2026\n   319→- **Category:** Project Management\n   320→\n   321→### [rtk](https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk)\n   322→CLI proxy that reduces LLM token consumption by 60-90% on common dev commands.\n   323→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   324→- **Category:** Token Optimization\n   325→\n   326→### [codeburn](https://github.com/getagentseal/codeburn)\n   327→Local tool tracking token usage and cost across 31 AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini.\n   328→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   329→- **Category:** Cost Tracking\n   330→\n   331→### [awesome-ai-tokenomics](https://github.com/QuesmaOrg/awesome-ai-tokenomics)\n   332→A map of what AI tokens actually cost, and where they're wasted vs. well spent.\n   333→- **Launch Date:** July 17, 2026\n   334→- **Category:** Cost Optimization/Research\n   335→\n   336→### [ruvnet/ruflo](https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo)\n   337→Multi-agent harness for deploying swarms, coordinating workflows, with adaptive memory and RAG integration.\n   338→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   339→- **Category:** Swarm Orchestration\n   340→\n   341→### [oraios/serena](https://github.com/oraios/serena)\n   342→MCP toolkit providing semantic retrieval and editing capabilities, described as \"the IDE for your agent\".\n   343→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   344→- **Category:** Agent IDE/Toolkit\n   345→\n   346→### [agno](https://github.com/agno-agi/agno)\n   347→Platform to \"build, run, and manage agent platforms\".\n   348→- **Launch Date:** July 29, 2026\n   349→- **Category:** Agent Platform\n   350→\n   351→### [tirth8205/code-review-graph](https://github.com/tirth8205/code-review-graph)\n   352→Local-first code intelligence graph for MCP and CLI building persistent maps of codebases.\n   353→- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n   354→- **Category:** Code Analysis/Graph\n   355→\n   356→### [yvgude/lean-ctx](https://github.com/yvgude/lean-ctx)\n   357→Context intelligence layer deciding \"what they read, remembers what they learn\" with 60-90% fewer tokens.\n   358→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   359→- **Category:** Context Optimization\n   360→\n   361→### [metalbear-co/mirrord](https://github.com/metalbear-co/mirrord)\n   362→Runs processes on local machines or AI agent environments as if in Kubernetes pods.\n   363→- **Launch Date:** July 28, 2026\n   364→- **Category:** DevOps/Cloud Integration\n   365→\n   366→---\n   367→\n   368→## MCP Server Ecosystem (July 15-29, 2026)\n   369→\n   370→### [livetennisapi-mcp](https://github.com/livetennisapi/livetennisapi-mcp)\n   371→MCP server for the Live Tennis API — give Claude, Cursor and other LLM agents real-time tennis scores, odds and model win-probability.\n   372→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   373→\n   374→### [Stormy Social Data API](https://github.com/OneInterface/stormy-cookbook)\n   375→Open-source cookbook for the Stormy Social Data API and MCP server — one REST API for TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, LinkedIn, X (Twitter), and Reddit.\n   376→- **Launch Date:** July 27, 2026\n   377→\n   378→### [App Store Connect MCP](https://github.com/erayendes/app-store-connect-mcp)\n   379→Heimdall — MCP server for the Apple App Store Connect API & App Store Server API (StoreKit 2). 982 tools from Apple's official OpenAPI spec.\n   380→- **Launch Date:** July 19, 2026\n   381→\n   382→### [Godot MCP Go](https://github.com/regiellis/godot-mcp-go)\n   383→Control a running Godot 4.7 editor and game directly from the terminal. Includes a Go CLI, editor addon, 312 commands, and an MCP server.\n   384→- **Launch Date:** July 23, 2026\n   385→\n   386→### [symbolpeek-mcp](https://github.com/pioner92/symbolpeek-mcp)\n   387→Token-efficient MCP server giving AI coding agents symbol-level reads of TS/JS, Rust, Python, Java, Go, JSON, and Markdown.\n   388→- **Launch Date:** July 20, 2026\n   389→\n   390→### [mcpgrade](https://github.com/TengByte/mcpgrade)\n   391→Lighthouse for MCP servers — score any MCP server on agent usability, not just spec compliance.\n   392→- **Launch Date:** July 18, 2026\n   393→\n   394→---\n   395→\n   396→## Summary Statistics\n   397→\n   398→- **Total Tools Discovered:** 80+ AI coding tools\n   399→- **Open-Source Projects:** ~90%\n   400→- **Most Active Launch Dates:** July 15, 17, 18, 20-22, 24, 28-29\n   401→- **Primary Categories:**\n   402→  1. CLI/Terminal Agents (15+ tools)\n   403→  2. Open-Source Agent Frameworks (12+ tools)\n   404→  3. Workflow Orchestration (10+ tools)\n   405→  4. IDE Integrations (8+ tools)\n   406→  5. Memory/Context Tools (6+ tools)\n   407→  6. Security/Governance (5+ tools)\n   408→  7. MCP Servers (15+ tools)\n   409→\n   410→## Key Trends\n   411→\n   412→1. **Terminal-based AI agents** are exploding as a category\n   413→2. **Multi-agent orchestration** is becoming mainstream\n   414→3. **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** ecosystem is rapidly expanding\n   415→4. **Cost optimization** tools (token tracking, smart routing) are emerging\n   416→5. **Memory persistence** across agent sessions is a major focus\n   417→6. **Security and governance** tooling is maturing\n   418→7. **Workflow standardization** through templates and playbooks\n   419→\n   420→---\n   421→\n   422→**